skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic.md:98: section outside the set: Commands
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic.md:20: list step in heading model: 1. Identify each prerequisite the supplied initiative row names.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic.md:21: list step in heading model: 2. Apply the initiative's [whole-epic dependency rule](initiative-issue-body.md#work-breakdown); a task row's reference to a row of another epic gates that row rather than this epic.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic.md:22: list step in heading model: 3. Confirm each prerequisite epic is closed as completed and every one of its bases has merged. Missing records leave the prerequisite unconfirmed.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic.md:23: list step in heading model: 4. Return the [Prerequisite Evidence](#prerequisite-evidence), identifying each confirmed prerequisite and missing condition. Only a confirmed result permits an unstarted epic's bases to be created or its task to be dispatched.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic.md:31: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Match Pull Requests](#match-pull-requests) with the epic JSON, pull request records as `--prs` and link snapshot as `--links`, supplying a local scratch output body as `--fix`.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic.md:32: indented detail in heading model: - A closed epic is normalized to the current Work Breakdown columns before its tasks are read, using the shared format rules. Ambiguous or unsupported table content is a blocker.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic.md:33: indented detail in heading model: - Publish reported table normalization through [Save Tracker Issue](issue.md#save-tracker-issue), fetch the saved epic and repeat the match before returning its evidence.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic.md:34: list step in heading model: 2. Return the [Delivery Findings](#delivery-findings); missing linked pull requests are missing evidence for the caller to supply.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic.md:42: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Inspect Epic Delivery](#inspect-epic-delivery) with the supplied epic JSON, pull request records and complete issue-link snapshot.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic.md:43: list step in heading model: 2. Confirm every task is delivered, every epic criterion is verified and ticked, and no open question or unresolved delivery discrepancy remains. An unmerged epic base awaiting integration is expected at this stage. Missing or stale verification leaves readiness unconfirmed.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic.md:44: list step in heading model: 3. Return the integration readiness in [Delivery State](#delivery-state), with the evidence revisions and each blocker. Readiness establishes the epic's content conditions; the caller supplies pull-request review, target and head-check evidence for the merge.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic.md:52: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Check Epic Readiness](#check-epic-readiness) with the current epic, pull request records, issue-link snapshot and criterion verification evidence.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic.md:53: list step in heading model: 2. Reconcile the expected bases with the task delivery targets.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic.md:54: list step in heading model: 3. Confirm every base has merged into its corresponding long-lived branch. An unknown or incomplete base list, or missing merge evidence, leaves completion unconfirmed even when every task is delivered and every criterion is ticked.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic.md:55: list step in heading model: 4. Return the completion result in [Delivery State](#delivery-state), identifying remaining blockers. Passing normal delivery checks supplies the caller's closure evidence; the tracker issue's current Development-link gate still governs the write.
