skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:280: section outside the set: Commands
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:25: list step in heading model: 1. Populate the body from the [Template](#template) at the supplied output path.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:26: indented detail in heading model: - Every section must meet [Fields](#fields).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:27: indented detail in heading model: - Shared content must meet the common [body conditions](issue-body.md#fields).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:28: list step in heading model: 2. Populate the shared table through [Write Issue Table](issue-body.md#write-issue-table).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:29: list step in heading model: 3. Fill the epic-specific cells.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:30: indented detail in heading model: - Each row must meet [Work Breakdown](#work-breakdown).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:31: indented detail in heading model: - Call [Assign Task Lanes](lane.md#assign-task-lanes) with the populated body, confirmed task-to-index map and output path.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:32: list step in heading model: 4. Call [Build Body Snapshot](issue-body.md#build-body-snapshot) with the draft body, title, labels and existing issue JSON when present.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:33: list step in heading model: 5. Pass that snapshot, initiative context, available pull request records, project checkout, evaluated revision and output file to [Validate Epic Body](#validate-epic-body).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:34: list step in heading model: 6. Identify unresolved publication links separately; they remain pending until tracker identities exist.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:35: list step in heading model: 7. Return the draft rows, their dependency references and the validation findings for the caller's cross-body ordering check.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:43: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Sync Epic](#sync-epic), mapping pull requests to `--prs`, links to `--links`, task issues to `--tasks`, each confirmed match to `--link`, the checkout to `--project`, each fetched epic base to a `--revision` and the output file to `--fix`.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:44: indented detail in heading model: - Row changes must meet [Task Delivery](#task-delivery) and [Work Breakdown](#work-breakdown).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:45: list step in heading model: 2. Return the updated body and [Delivery Findings](epic.md#delivery-findings) for the caller to resolve and publish. An unmerged epic base prevents a closable result.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:53: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Tick Epic Criteria](#tick-epic-criteria) with the epic JSON, records as `--prs`, snapshot as `--links`, verified ids as `--tick` and output as `--fix`. Refuse criteria not ready to verify.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:54: list step in heading model: 2. Return the body and refused criteria.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:62: list step in heading model: 1. Require the caller's confirmed unit and existing planning folder. Refuse a row already held or linked to a pull request or commit, and a unit [Work Units](delivery-plan.md#work-units) does not admit.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:63: list step in heading model: 2. Run [Reserve Row](#reserve-row) with the epic as `--epic`, every id of the unit as `--reserve`, the board items as `--items`, supplied base URL as `--records`, record date as `--date` and output as `--fix`.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:64: list step in heading model: 3. Return the reserved body meeting [Task Delivery](#task-delivery).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:72: list step in heading model: 1. Require the supplied release decision and refuse any row that is not held.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:73: list step in heading model: 2. Run [Release Row](#release-row) with the epic as `--epic`, every id of each released unit as `--release`, the engineering worktree as `--engineering` and output as `--fix`.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:74: list step in heading model: 3. Return the released body meeting [Task Delivery](#task-delivery).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:82: list step in heading model: 1. Read the changed paths of each epic pull request reaching a branch the project's [Required Criteria](#required-criteria) declare, through [Read Pull Request State](pull-request.md#read-pull-request-state).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:83: list step in heading model: 2. Call [Validate Issue Body](issue-body.md#validate-issue-body) with the current body, local [Fields](#fields), supplied related evidence and output file, supplying initiative JSON as `--initiative`, pull requests as `--prs`, each pull request's changed paths as `--files <number>=<changed-paths-file>`, the checkout as `--project` and the revision as `--revision`.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:84: indented detail in heading model: - The evaluated revision is the epic's base on the long-lived branch that holds the project's configuration, such as `origin/i07/e00/workspace`, or that branch itself, such as `origin/workspace`, while the epic has no base on it. Fetch it before the check reads it.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:85: list step in heading model: 3. Read reach from each epic pull request's base, through an epic base or initiative branch. Without pull requests, no criterion is lacking.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:86: list step in heading model: 4. Include in the findings each [Required Criteria](#required-criteria) criterion an epic lacks whose work changes the criterion's paths on its branch, required criteria the declaration or the changed paths leave unevaluable, and any epic criterion no task row delivers.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:87: list step in heading model: 5. Return the corrected body, mechanical diff and unresolved findings for the caller.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:95: list step in heading model: 1. Apply the confirmed row changes through [Populate Epic Issue Body](#populate-epic-issue-body), preserving unrelated content.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:96: indented detail in heading model: - Description, Coverage, Depends on, Joins, Lane and task grain must meet [Work Breakdown](#work-breakdown).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:97: indented detail in heading model: - Split a task exceeding the allowed criterion grain into the confirmed tasks.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:98: list step in heading model: 2. Return the revised body and any cross-body numbering or dependency changes for the caller.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:106: list step in heading model: 1. Present each unmet criterion and its missing evidence to the user.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:107: indented detail in heading model: - Return the criteria the user confirms already hold to the caller for verification and ticking. The delivered task retains them.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:108: indented detail in heading model: - Record an unanswered decision as pending.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:109: indented detail in heading model: - If no criteria need further work, return the pending findings to the caller.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:110: indented detail in heading model: - Continue to the draft step with only the criteria the user confirms need further work.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:111: list step in heading model: 2. Draft a further task for the criteria selected for further work, meeting [Work Breakdown](#work-breakdown).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:112: indented detail in heading model: - Confirm the draft with the user.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:113: indented detail in heading model: - On acceptance, call [Revise Epic Rows](#revise-epic-rows) with the further row and the criteria it adopts from the delivered task's Coverage.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:114: indented detail in heading model: - Return an unanswered draft as pending without continuing to the reconcile step.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:115: list step in heading model: 3. Run [Record Epic Delivery](#record-epic-delivery) with the revised epic, the supplied delivery evidence, the project checkout and the fetched epic bases.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:116: indented detail in heading model: - Publish the returned body through [Save Tracker Issue](issue.md#save-tracker-issue).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/epic-issue-body.md:117: indented detail in heading model: - Return the saved row and criterion disposition to the caller.
