skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:113: section outside the set: Commands
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:25: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Select Tracker Number](issue.md#select-tracker-number) with the hot-fix prefix letter.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:26: list step in heading model: 2. Run [Ensure Repository Labels](repository-labels.md#ensure-repository-labels) with the labels hot-fix [Titles](hotfix-body.md#titles) name.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:27: list step in heading model: 3. Return the hot-fix number to the caller, which rewrites and saves the issue's body, title and labels, then places it through [Settle Hot-fix Board Status](#settle-hot-fix-board-status), as its [placement](placement.md#disposition-conditions) orders.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:35: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Record Dispatch Status](board-delivery.md#record-dispatch-status) with the hot-fix issue for In Progress and the supplied board evidence. That status is the hold [Delivery Unit](#delivery-unit) defines.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:36: list step in heading model: 2. Return the confirmed status, or the discrepancy, to the caller. The session starts only once it is confirmed.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:44: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Capture Issue Development](issue.md#capture-issue-development) for the hot-fix issue.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:45: indented detail in heading model: - Refuse the release while its [Delivery Unit](#delivery-unit) is running or unrecorded, and return the pull request that makes it so to the caller.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:46: list step in heading model: 2. Run [Place Issue on Board](board.md#place-issue-on-board) with the supplied board, the hot-fix issue and Ready.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:47: list step in heading model: 3. Return the saved item and its Status to the caller.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:55: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Sync Hot-fix Issue](#sync-hot-fix-issue) with the hot-fix JSON, records as `--prs`, snapshot as `--links`, delivery number as `--pr`, verified ids as `--tick` and output as `--fix`. Tick only criteria the caller has verified.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:56: list step in heading model: 2. Return the body and eligibility findings; the caller publishes the body and closes the tracker issue, as [Delivery Record](#delivery-record) states.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:64: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Read Tracker Issue](issue.md#read-tracker-issue) for the hot-fix's current state.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:65: list step in heading model: 2. Run [Read Board State](board.md#read-board-state) for its item and Status. A hot-fix with no item has no Status.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:66: list step in heading model: 3. Apply the status [Board Status](#board-status) gives that state and Status:
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:67: indented detail in heading model: - **A status.**
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:68: indented detail in heading model: - Run [Place Issue on Board](board.md#place-issue-on-board) with the supplied board, the hot-fix issue and that status, which adds the item where the board has none.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:69: indented detail in heading model: - **Off the board, with an item.**
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:70: indented detail in heading model: - Run [Remove Board Item](board.md#remove-board-item) with the supplied board owner and number and the item id Read Board State returned.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:71: indented detail in heading model: - **Off the board, with no item.**
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:72: indented detail in heading model: - Change nothing; the hot-fix already stands off the board.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/hotfix.md:73: list step in heading model: 4. Return the settled item, its removal, or the unchanged board to the caller.
