skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:196: section outside the set: Commands
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:21: list step in heading model: 1. Populate the body through [Draft Initiative Issue Body](#draft-initiative-issue-body).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:22: list step in heading model: 2. Follow [Check Round of Edits](issue-body.md#check-round-of-edits).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:23: list step in heading model: 3. Return the populated body and its local format findings to the caller.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:31: list step in heading model: 1. Populate the body from the [Template](#template) into a local file at the supplied output path.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:32: indented detail in heading model: - That file must be the source for every later edit.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:33: indented detail in heading model: - All populated fields must meet [Fields](#fields).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:34: list step in heading model: 2. Derive the Problem and Non-Goals from the proposal this initiative is scoped to.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:35: indented detail in heading model: - The Problem must meet [Problem and Proposal](issue-body.md#problem-and-proposal).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:36: indented detail in heading model: - Each Non-Goal must meet [Non-Goals](#non-goals).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:37: list step in heading model: 3. Write the acceptance criteria before the Work Breakdown, so each row's Coverage can cite them.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:38: indented detail in heading model: - Each criterion must come from a confirmed clause and meet [Initiative Acceptance Criteria](#initiative-acceptance-criteria).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:39: indented detail in heading model: - The criteria must come from the requirements sources the proposal references. Where the proposal references none, they must come from the proposal's body alone.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:40: list step in heading model: 4. Populate the shared table through [Write Issue Table](issue-body.md#write-issue-table).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:41: list step in heading model: 5. Fill the initiative-specific cells.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:42: indented detail in heading model: - Each row must meet [Work Breakdown](#work-breakdown).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:43: indented detail in heading model: - An item a test cannot observe must stay named as [Coverage Reports](issue-body.md#coverage-reports) define.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:51: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Sync Initiative](#sync-initiative) with the initiative and all linked epic records as `--epics`, supplying `--fix` when an output body is requested.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:52: list step in heading model: 2. Return the body and [Delivery Findings](initiative.md#delivery-findings) from the supplied initiative and epic records. Delivery eligibility follows [Delivery State](initiative.md#delivery-state).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:60: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Tick Initiative Criteria](#tick-initiative-criteria) with the initiative, linked epics as `--epics`, verified ids as `--tick` and output as `--fix`. Refuse criteria not ready to verify.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:61: list step in heading model: 2. Return the body and refused criteria.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:69: list step in heading model: 1. Call [Validate Issue Body](issue-body.md#validate-issue-body) with the current body, local [Fields](#fields), supplied related evidence and output file, supplying each linked epic as `--epic`.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:70: list step in heading model: 2. Use its current title for the initiative row.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:71: list step in heading model: 3. Include excluded names in Problem and Proposal and criterion/source departures in the findings.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:72: list step in heading model: 4. Return the corrected body, mechanical diff and unresolved findings for the caller.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:80: list step in heading model: 1. Read each local source at its checkout path.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:81: list step in heading model: 2. For a pinned GitHub blob, run [Fetch Source](#fetch-source) with its repository, path, pinned revision and output file.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:82: list step in heading model: 3. Fetch other URLs through the harness's web access.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:83: list step in heading model: 4. Record an unreadable or empty source as a [Sources](#sources) finding; its criteria remain unevaluated.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md:84: list step in heading model: 5. Return each source's contents and identity with those findings.
