skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:168: section outside the set: Commands
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:13: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Fetch Tracker Issue](#fetch-tracker-issue) for the complete JSON, or [Fetch Issue Body](#fetch-issue-body) for its body, with the issue number and destination file.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:14: list step in heading model: 2. Run [Fetch Issue Comments](#fetch-issue-comments) when the request depends on the discussion.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:22: list step in heading model: 1. Take the supplied body and metadata, preserving each field the caller does not change for an existing issue.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:23: list step in heading model: 2. Return a missing-label result when an assignment names a label the repository does not contain.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:24: list step in heading model: 3. For a new issue, run [Create Tracker Issue](#create-tracker-issue) with the body's file, title and labels.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:25: list step in heading model: 4. For an existing issue, run [Patch Issue Body](#patch-issue-body), [Retitle Tracker Issue](#retitle-tracker-issue), [Add Issue Labels](#add-issue-labels) or [Remove Issue Label](#remove-issue-label) for the fields being changed.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:26: list step in heading model: 5. Run [Comment on Issue](#comment-on-issue) for an answer the caller requires, with the issue number and comment file.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:27: list step in heading model: 6. Re-read with [Fetch Tracker Issue](#fetch-tracker-issue).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:28: list step in heading model: 7. Compare the saved fields with the intended body and metadata.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:36: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Capture Issue Development](#capture-issue-development) for the issue's current JSON and its Development snapshot.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:37: indented detail in heading model: - The issue's entire Development field establishes membership, across repositories and states. Titles, branch names, body mentions and a list filtered to one initiative do not. An empty field adds no pull request requirement.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:38: list step in heading model: 2. Run [Check Issue Closure](#check-issue-closure) with those two files.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:39: list step in heading model: 3. Require normal delivery checks to pass, every criterion to be verified and ticked, and every currently linked pull request to be merged.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:40: indented detail in heading model: - Keep the issue open for an open, draft or closed-without-merge linked pull request, and for links never read.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:41: indented detail in heading model: - Return an abandoned or incorrect Development link to the caller for the user's decision on its removal. A replacement pull request does not remove the requirement on a link still present.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:42: list step in heading model: 4. Run [Close as Completed](#close-as-completed), which repeats the gate immediately before the write.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:50: list step in heading model: 1. Confirm the supplied destination contains the work and cites its source issue.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:51: list step in heading model: 2. Run [Comment on Issue](#comment-on-issue) with the destination reference and supplied comment file.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:52: list step in heading model: 3. Run [Close as Not Planned](#close-as-not-planned), retaining the issue's body.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:53: list step in heading model: 4. Re-read it with [Fetch Tracker Issue](#fetch-tracker-issue) to confirm its state and reason.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:61: list step in heading model: 1. When replying to feedback already folded into the body, compose a precise, factual reply addressing each point and mentioning the reviewer, with no thanks or filler. Name what the body now says, by criterion id where one carries it, or the issue that takes the point.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:62: list step in heading model: 2. Publish the supplied comment:
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:63: indented detail in heading model: - For a one-line comment, run [Post Inline Comment](#post-inline-comment) with the exact text.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:64: indented detail in heading model: - For a longer comment, run [Post Comment File](#post-comment-file) with the complete file.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:65: list step in heading model: 3. Return the saved comment URL.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:73: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Capture Issue Development](#capture-issue-development) immediately before closure with the issue identity, authenticated access and evidence paths.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:74: list step in heading model: 2. Run [Check Issue Closure](#check-issue-closure) with the issue and Development files it wrote, using absolute evidence paths when changing directory.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:75: list step in heading model: 3. Require exit 0 and passing normal delivery checks; a sync report of closable does not permit skipping this gate.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:76: list step in heading model: 4. Immediately after the gate passes, run [Set Completed State](#set-completed-state) with the issue's repository and number and the passing evidence.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:77: list step in heading model: 5. Return the saved state or failure.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:85: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Fetch Tracker Issue](#fetch-tracker-issue) into `issue-943.json` or the supplied path.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:86: list step in heading model: 2. Run [Read Issue Development](#read-issue-development) with that file, saving `links-943.json` or the supplied path. An unreadable relation writes no snapshot, which blocks the caller; an empty array means the field was read and is empty.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:87: list step in heading model: 3. Return both files, or the unreadable relation.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:95: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Capture Issue Links](#capture-issue-links) with the supplied issues and destination.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:96: list step in heading model: 2. Return each issue's observed pull requests, or stop and return each unreadable relation the capture names as a blocker.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:104: list step in heading model: 1. Fetch the closed issues alone:
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:105: indented detail in heading model: - For named issues, run [Fetch Selected Closed Issues](#fetch-selected-closed-issues) with their numbers.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:106: indented detail in heading model: - For the whole repository, run [Fetch Closed Issues](#fetch-closed-issues).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:107: indented detail in heading model: - An empty collection means none of the named issues is closed; return nothing listed.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:108: list step in heading model: 2. Run [Read Issue Development](#read-issue-development) with that collection; an unreadable relation is returned as a blocker and the sweep does not run.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:109: list step in heading model: 3. Run [Sweep Closure Evidence](#sweep-closure-evidence) with the collection and the issue-links file.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:110: list step in heading model: 4. Return each unsupported issue with its state reason and findings, and each unevaluable issue as missing evidence, as findings. Return the not-planned closures apart, as listed for reference. The audit changes no issue.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:118: list step in heading model: 1. Read the setting where the authenticated API exposes it, and take a read value as the answer.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:119: list step in heading model: 2. Where no API field carries it, put the setting to the user and take their explicit answer, meeting [Auto-Close Setting](#auto-close-setting).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:120: list step in heading model: 3. Return the confirmed value. An unconfirmed setting is a blocker, and an enabled one leaves the caller to obtain authorization before the repository is reconfigured.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:128: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Fetch All Issues](#fetch-all-issues), saving the complete collection.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:129: list step in heading model: 2. Return it with pull requests distinguishable from issues.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:137: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Find Initiative Issue](#find-initiative-issue) with the supplied repository and prefix.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:138: list step in heading model: 2. Return its issue number or an unresolved identity.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:146: list step in heading model: 1. Run [List Prefixed Titles](#list-prefixed-titles) for the supplied repository and prefix letter, covering all issue states.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:147: list step in heading model: 2. Read the highest prefix carrying that letter.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:148: list step in heading model: 3. Confirm the following number, or `00` when there is no prefix, remains unused before creation.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue.md:149: list step in heading model: 4. Return the confirmed number.
