skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:20: list step in heading model: 1. Populate the shared Done, Coverage and Depends on cells from the supplied row data.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:21: indented detail in heading model: - The columns must match the kind's table.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:22: indented detail in heading model: - The shared cells must meet [Tables](#tables).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:23: list step in heading model: 2. Read the finished table against [Tables](#tables), [Numbering](#numbering), and [Reference form](#reference-form).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:31: list step in heading model: 1. Check each section of the issue against the field conditions for its kind and against [Fields](#fields) in this file.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:32: list step in heading model: 2. Run [Check Body Format](#check-body-format) on every issue the round changed.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:40: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Check Body Format](#check-body-format) with the supplied issue JSON, kind inputs and output file as `--fix`.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:41: list step in heading model: 2. Review the body against the supplied field conditions.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:42: list step in heading model: 3. Return the [Format Findings](#format-findings).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:50: list step in heading model: 1. Populate missing sections from the supplied issue and related context.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:51: list step in heading model: 2. Apply each confirmed decision to keep, fold or remove an extra section, and rewrite a wrong-kind body in the selected template.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:52: list step in heading model: 3. Record a required tracker-kind change for the caller.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:53: list step in heading model: 4. Restate historical narration as the current design.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:54: list step in heading model: 5. Apply confirmed criterion changes.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:55: indented detail in heading model: - The body must meet [Body](#body), [Shared Acceptance Criteria](#shared-acceptance-criteria) and the supplied kind conditions.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:56: list step in heading model: 6. Validate the body through [Validate Issue Body](#validate-issue-body).
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:57: list step in heading model: 7. Return the corrected file, validation findings and any required cross-body or metadata changes for the caller.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:65: list step in heading model: 1. Write the body's exact text, title and labels to the destination as JSON.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:66: list step in heading model: 2. Preserve the existing issue's identity and state when supplied.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:67: list step in heading model: 3. For an unpublished draft, use `number: null` and `state: "open"`; labels are strings or objects with a name.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:68: list step in heading model: 4. Return the JSON path for validation. No tracker issue is created by this operation.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:76: list step in heading model: 1. Run [Validate Issue Body](#validate-issue-body) with the supplied JSON, kind conditions, related evidence and output path.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:77: indented detail in heading model: - Return an unreadable source as a blocker before editing.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:78: list step in heading model: 2. Review the returned diff.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:79: indented detail in heading model: - Publish wording-preserving format, title and label corrections through [Save Tracker Issue](issue.md#save-tracker-issue), without asking.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:80: indented detail in heading model: - Retain content decisions and cross-body findings separately; do not publish them as mechanical fixes.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:81: list step in heading model: 3. Resolve a non-mechanical finding confined to this body.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:82: indented detail in heading model: - Obtain the user's decision.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:83: indented detail in heading model: - Run [Apply Body Corrections](#apply-body-corrections) with the current body, kind template and conditions, related context, confirmed resolution and output path.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:84: indented detail in heading model: - Publish through Save Tracker Issue. An unanswered decision or a finding requiring changes to other issues returns to the caller as a blocker.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:85: list step in heading model: 4. Run [Read Tracker Issue](issue.md#read-tracker-issue) for the saved issue.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:86: indented detail in heading model: - Repeat Validate Issue Body with the saved JSON and the same kind conditions, context and output path.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:87: indented detail in heading model: - Return the saved body, whether a correction was made, and the validation result to the caller. A remaining failure is a blocker.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:95: list step in heading model: 1. Run [List Reference Repositories](#list-reference-repositories) to identify the destination and cited repositories.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:96: list step in heading model: 2. Run [Fetch Reference Repository](#fetch-reference-repository) for each returned name; collect the returned objects into a JSON array at the snapshot path. Retain failed fetches as unresolved visibility, never as public visibility.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:97: list step in heading model: 3. Run [Validate Reference Visibility](#validate-reference-visibility) with that snapshot and the issue record.
skills/work-planner/artifacts/issue-body.md:98: list step in heading model: 4. Return each private reference on a public issue and each unavailable visibility as a finding. A private destination has no public-reference restriction; deciding how to replace or remove a private reference belongs to the caller.
